was a personal humiliation for the 80-year-old Trump, leaving him as a lame duck president for the remaining two years of his term. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Global travel sector grows despite headwinds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284dcfa6cf4a463099ca3e99cc909e9c32f0338cf0774615da9bb706a9c28807</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:43:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261105-global-travel-sector-grows-despite-headwinds" /><summary type="html">The global tourism sector is growing, despite conflicts and economic uncertainty. That's the finding of a new report by World Travel Market, which says the number of international arrivals is set to hit a record 1.57 billion in 2026.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>Europe: Dozens of flights diverted following bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a10375269a1c9724055da1d000603a831071253d5f945753679fc74d5ea97810</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:40:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-europe-dozens-of-flights-diverted-following-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Hoax bomb threats hit at least 27 affected flights around Europe this week.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Identity crisis': Can Democrats 'deliver' following their 'historic', once in a generation victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e4cae9ba8769a7cef2b5fd922ada74c3d8f1cce582d8876f94d3ed3ef11d3c</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:27:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/identity-crisis-can-democrats-deliver-following-their-historic-once-in-a-generation-victory" /><summary type="html">A historic Democratic electoral breakthrough has transformed the American political landscape. For Laurie Dundon, Senior Associate Fellow at the European Leadership Network and former US diplomat, the central question is whether the Democratic Party can convert electoral momentum into coherent governance. "Can they deliver?" Dunden examines the apparent disintegration of Donald Trump's 2024 MAGA coalition alongside the Democratic Party's continuing ideological struggle between its progressive and centrist wings. Ahead of 2028, Dunden cautions against seeing Trump as a lame duck: "Trump is never going to stop being Trump." The resulting struggle over congressional spending powers, presidential vetoes, tariffs and investigations promises to be a delicate dance to watch".</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's main Arab list backs Eisenkot to form government after election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b3a217a92516f48ab7d5429111f499ccd4336d6d4332247d9eb62c8bcaab863</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:43:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's largest Arab party grouping said Thursday it would recommend opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government, potentially bolstering his bid after Arab-majority lists won a record 19 seats in last week's election and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lost the support of an allied religious party.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Bringing the magic of Harry Potter to life through music</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5be4b83cfef1df705001e57b56f1ef3f87ed56687787d33e0bc53aac3175350</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:30:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261105-bringing-the-magic-of-harry-potter-to-life-through-music" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Entre Nous, we meet Timothy Henty, the British conductor bringing the magic of Harry Potter to life in Paris. As part of the Harry Potter Film Concert Series, he leads more than 80 musicians in a spectacular live orchestral performance, offering audiences a unique opportunity to experience one of cinema's most beloved stories like never before.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>British comedian Russell Brand found guilty of rape, sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6950bfff5e5a4e2259acebb494fcd80dea7974984e8c69a30a0325149a8aa02b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:26:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261105-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-sexual-assault" /><summary type="html">A London jury on Thursday convicted British comedian and actor Russell Brand of one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France faces new protests as government seeks to prevent violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8df3ddb1483fe36198d8390011b7c7b735012f18ef9b01bbebddc56bbfb213f</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:19:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-faces-new-protests-as-government-seeks-to-prevent-violence" /><summary type="html">France faces new protests as the government seeks to prevent a repeat of October unrest. Protesters demand better public services, including education, and also critique the rising cost-of-living. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>French bank hit by cyberattack, hackers steal $100 million</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1e6231c78bd7e9b4b2f67242fede5918f731202088eedc363ad3794be8eda3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:09:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cyberattack-french-bank-says-online-hacking-stole-around-100-million" /><summary type="html">French regional bank Crédit Mutuel Arkéa said Wednesday it had been hit by a cyberattack that led to fraudulent transfers worth around 100 million euros ($112 million). The bank said the attack, which has since been "contained", allowed hackers to access its own accounts and transfer funds to other banks. Customer accounts were not affected, and no losses were reported by clients.</summary></entry><entry><title>South African star Zolani Mahola: From 'Waka Waka' with Shakira to 'People Power'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa1b9ed95c33ba0c2cdca2096f7a24ffd5d668af202367588af6b75a40c9122c</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:34:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261105-south-african-star-zolani-mahola-from-waka-waka-with-shakira-to-people-power" /><summary type="html">From the global success of "Waka Waka" to her forthcoming second solo album "People Power", South Africa's Zolani Mahola has built a career around the power of music to bring people together.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>'It's fascinating to see a human becoming a person': Author Clémentine Goldszal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e25e7a8e0a5f00e0adf0142e83185bd83c1959d7acb47a9b0395b0b2758a54a</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261105-it-s-fascinating-to-see-a-human-becoming-a-person-author-cl%C3%A9mentine-goldszal" /><summary type="html">What is life like for a newly born, premature or sick baby? These are the questions tackled by a French journalist in her first ever book. Clémentine Goldszal asks what it means to be rushed from the delivery room to the neonatal intensive care unit, and what is means to enter the world before you are ready. Goldszal's book is entitled "Newborn: Inside the World of Neonatal Care". She spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Bent on leaving his mark: Trump's proposed 'Triumphal Arch' sparks backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b5a0c87c2447695e114326e3668cbfcad3339b5e99735b8f1097e4f8959bb3c</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:55:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261105-bent-on-leaving-his-mark-trump-s-proposed-triumphal-arch-sparks-backlash" /><summary type="html">Since his return to power, US President Donald Trump has been intent on reshaping the nation's capital Washington, seeking to leave his name and mark on it. After his involvement with the Kennedy Center, the White House ballroom and the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool, Trump is now particularly keen on building a 250-foot (79-metre) "Triumphal Arch" – a project he claims is intended to honour the 250th anniversary of the United States.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>What comes next for Democrats after midterm election victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e15a1f55e9b47db82b8c1b6da1ccb859c9cae004aa95233ffbe47e03b3d55edb</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:54:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-what-comes-next-for-democrats-after-midterm-election-victory" /><summary type="html">With the US midterms over, Democrats are turning to what could become one of their most crowded and unpredictable presidential primaries in decades – a 2028 contest ​likely to expose the party's divide over how to win back the White House. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Multiple flights in Europe diverted because of bomb threats after earlier hoaxes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ff4163443e7702549bb9cd210f1840c30da1daa70686896fbc7885c76e4d932</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-multiple-flights-in-europe-diverted-because-of-bomb-threats-after-earlier-hoaxes" /><summary type="html">Multiple flights in Europe made emergency landings on Thursday after being diverted because of bomb threats. The incidents followed hoax bomb threats earlier this week that prompted searches, diversions and in one case a military escort.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: High schools blocked again as students reject government responses as 'meaningless'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3659603a3c291fac295f0b6798e07d8798b947a1174e87d029ec0a7c2cfbc6a9</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:51:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-france-high-schools-blocked-again-as-students-reject-government-responses-as-meaningless" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 Students are blocking their schools and universities across France again this Thursday, November 5, despite the government’s response, which they deem insufficient.</summary></entry><entry><title>Farewell Botox, heels and big hair: Is this the end of MAGA women?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83fb8e7844453e72b774787b7ad900f9e77a7567966a5b77356027cc0b826028</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:15:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261105-farewell-botox-heels-and-big-hair-is-this-the-end-of-maga-women" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, November 5: "Loser" and "Reborn in the USA" are just some of the headlines dominating the international press after the Democrats stomped to victory in the US midterm elections. What impact will their success have on the rest of Donald Trump's presidency? How will he govern with a Democratic-controlled Congress? These are just some of the burning questions after that vote. Also, do the midterm results signal the end of the MAGA woman and the "Mar-a-Lago face"?</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Bomb threats cause major flight disruptions across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2832e8d80409c06db6907331171fa5263579c3a37917ae1b2efd9e291098bdfd</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:32:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-bomb-threats-cause-major-flight-disruptions-across-europe" /><summary type="html">Bomb ​threats forced airliners to make unplanned landings across Europe on Thursday morning, the latest in a series of threats targeting flights in Europe. While no country has attributed blame for the threats, they come at a time ​when European officials have been blaming both Russia and Iran for what they describe as "hybrid attacks" and acts of sabotage. Moscow and Tehran both deny any such campaign. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Elon Musk fails $440 million bet as Republicans lose</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f600592300e9107c1d98eff88833f2e1fac8c3eb96be56f325643a6faf0287f</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:29:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-elon-musk-fails-440-million-bet-as-republicans-lose" /><summary type="html">The 2026 midterm elections were the most expensive on record, with nearly 12 billion dollars spent during the campaign. Tech tycoon Elon Musk was by far the largest individual donor ever, injecting over 440 million dollars of his money to support the GOP. Tuesday's resounding Democratic victory showed the limits of his money, power and influence.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist jailed for 10 more years for collusion with foreign forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a89417b2c30cecb40af28ccb8c49c448ab85b675012af6b082ef638c46094fdc</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:29:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-hong-kong-activist-jailed-for-10-more-years-for-collusion-with-foreign-forces" /><summary type="html">Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in jail on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, the second time he has been penalised under the city's national security law. Hong, 30, is one of the most globally recognised faces of Hong Kong's pro-democracy movement and has already spent almost six years behind bars. He is now not due for release until late 2036.</summary></entry><entry><title>Route du Rhum 2026: Sailors forced to abandon race for various reasons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:450148dba23c48c0b8013fa54d338b7025a2e381a428d5907682b095becd9867</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:25:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-route-du-rhum-2026-sailors-forced-to-abandon-race-for-various-reasons" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Route du Rhum is continuing to deliver one setback after another since Sunday’s start in Saint-Malo. From boats capsizing to sailors being forced to abandon the race, the favourites are dropping out one by one. But how do so many boats suffer damage so early in the race?</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Democrats say ready to negotiate and promise big changes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b28446716e86aa8160ccf0aa9008e5cbb0e7c876d30c4961fd324e361d49b63</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:22:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-democrats-say-ready-to-negotiate-and-promise-big-changes" /><summary type="html">US Democrats are promising to leverage their landslide election win to bring down living costs and hold President Donald Trump's administration to account. They are set to take control of both chambers of Congress in January, but delivering on their agenda could mean striking deals with the very president they have pledged to rein in.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthi missiles fired at Medina intercepted, Saudi coalition says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75a64664c417a81dc2e3f0866d4bdb0700df38585fcfd06a1f728027c6fffc95</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:07:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-houthi-missiles-fired-at-medina-intercepted-saudi-coalition-says" /><summary type="html">A ballistic missile fired at the Saudi city of Medina, one of Islam's holiest cities, was intercepted Thursday, a spokesman for the Saudi-led coalition fighting Yemen's Houthi rebels said. The announcement came shortly after the kingdom's civil defence agency warned of potential danger around the strategic port of Yanbu.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Football legend Cristiano Ronaldo announces international retirement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa8d14395bc22e98dd976d614e91538b2019de55cc4595c49dcf7222b278769d</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T10:48:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261105-football-legend-cristiano-ronaldo-announces-international-retirement" /></entry></feed>
